  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 336 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nWednesday through Monday:\n\nWisconsin remains on the northern edge of 500 mb ridging through\nthe end of the work week, with chances for convection/ridge \nriding MCSs through Friday and lingering high heat and humidity\nthrough Thursday. Individual 500 mb shortwaves and LLJs will be\nthe driving force for storms through the week, with exact \ntiming and placement likely not becoming clear until 24 hours \nfrom the each event. Currently, highest confidence in widespread\nstorm development for southern Wisconsin is Wednesday night \ninto Thursday, as broad low pressure develops in the central \nPlains and brings a stronger, more focused LLJ to eastern Iowa \nand southwestern Wisconsin. This would support a severe threat \ndue to the enhanced CAPE, moisture, and more focused trigger and\ntend to like the NBM 50-70% PoPs going into Thursday morning. \n\nAs low pressure deepens in the Northeast U.S. on Friday, high\npressure builds into Ontario, bringing drier, northeasterly flow\nto the Great Lakes and bringing a return to drier conditions and\nmore seasonable temperatures for the weekend into Monday (highs\nin the low 80s).\n\nMH",
